XR eye depth: the eyes' linear depth for the XR layer's reprojection (aurora_xr_set_eye_depth)

WakerQuest (rama reproyeccion). While the XR layer asks for it, each diorama frame (the diorama, the window,
the immersive mode) also carries its eyes' depth in an AHardwareBuffer of its own (AuroraXrFrame.depth), in the
colour's slot, written by the same submit and handed over with the same take/done and its own sync file. Each eye's
depth is written right after its mask (the EFB depth still its own), at half size, as the inverse of the distance
along the eye's view axis in metres of the room (the head's space, through the eye's own clip matrix), 16 bits over
R and G; 0 where nothing was drawn (infinitely far). Off by default: nothing drawn nor allocated while off.

